      "message": "This still provides the opportunity for plugins to mistakenly specify their name incorrectly and hence collide with other plugin\u0027s namespace. If we want to use `@PluginName` annotation we should do something like:\n\n```\npublic class PluginLockKeys {\n  private final String pluginName;\n\n  @Inject\n  PluginLockKeys(@PluginName String pluginName) {\n    this.pluginName \u003d pluginName;\n  }\n\n  public LockKey of(String name, String... args) {\n    return LockKey.plugin(pluginName, name, args);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nand then remove this method from here ? If two plugins want to share a namespace they could still do so by explicitly calling LockKey#of().\n\n@sasa.zivkov@sap.com Do you think its a valid concern and solution ?",
